From: ZaraOS <noreply@zaraos>
Subject: [PATCH] Add missing #include <limits>

cpptoml.h uses std::numeric_limits without including <limits>, which
fails to compile with GCC >= 11 (libstdc++ no longer pulls it in
transitively).

Upstream: https://github.com/skystrife/cpptoml/pull/123
---
 include/cpptoml.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/include/cpptoml.h
+++ b/include/cpptoml.h
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <cstring>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <iomanip>
+#include <limits>
 #include <map>
 #include <memory>
 #include <sstream>
